id: E547
trigger_tool: clang|as|make|test
phase: compilation|testing
error_signature: unknown pseudo-op.*\.addrsig|unknown directive.*\.addrsig
severity: 2
category: toolchain, compat, asm, portability, testing
match_keywords: Clang, GNU as, .addrsig, -fno-addrsig, assembly, integrated assembler
title: Clang address-significance directive rejected by GNU as
root_cause: Clang emits the LLVM .addrsig assembly directive by default, while the selected GNU as version does not parse that directive when a build or test passes compiler-generated assembly through GNU as.
affected_scope: Clang-built projects and toolchain tests that generate textual assembly and feed it to GNU as instead of the Clang integrated assembler.
verification_cmd: AS_BIN="${AS_BIN:-$(command -v as)}"; clang -S fixture.c -o default.s; ! "$AS_BIN" default.s -o default.o; clang -fno-addrsig -S fixture.c -o clean.s; "$AS_BIN" clean.s -o clean.o
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: suppress-clang-address-significance-directive
rec_description: When GNU as is intentionally the assembler under test, add -fno-addrsig through the build-system compiler flags so Clang omits only address-significance metadata while preserving generated code and all upstream tests.
rec_command: AS_BIN="${AS_BIN:-$(command -v as)}"; clang -fno-addrsig -S fixture.c -o clean.s; "$AS_BIN" clean.s -o clean.o
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: compiler-flags
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: use-clang-integrated-assembler
fallback_description: For ordinary builds that do not exercise GNU as behavior, keep the Clang integrated assembler so it consumes its own .addrsig directive.
fallback_command: clang -c fixture.c -o fixture.o
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: compiler-selection
forbid_1_pattern: skip.*assembler.*test|delete.*\.addrsig.*test
forbid_1_reason: Skipping the affected toolchain tests hides a compiler-to-assembler compatibility boundary.
forbid_1_consequence: The build may publish tools whose compiler-generated assembly path was never exercised.
principles: P006
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [E016]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
doc_file: drafts/E547-draft-61BA.md
last_updated: 2026-09-04
source_event: binutils 2.46.0 host probe: Clang 18 default assembly failed GNU as 2.46.0 on .addrsig; -fno-addrsig assembly succeeded.
authors: sawakage <sawakage@outlook.com>
